# LF in the working tree everywhere, matching CI (Linux) — this repo's artifacts are hashed, so a
# platform-dependent checkout is never harmless.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The published registry is *content-addressed*: index.json pins each bundle's SHA-256, and clients
# verify those exact bytes at install time. Git must not EOL-translate them at all — on a Windows
# checkout (core.autocrlf=true) the working-tree copy would hash differently than what
# raw.githubusercontent serves, which makes `publish:registry` trip its own version-immutability
# guard with phantom "content changed" errors. `-text` pins the bytes byte-for-byte.
bridges/** -text
index.json -text
